<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Elphinstone Erskine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1838–1911</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as James Erskine</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Elphinstone Erskine was a British naval officer. As commodore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> Station he proclaimed a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> over the south-eastern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-moresby">Port Moresby</a> in November 1884, the origin of British New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a> and later Papua. He later reached the rank of admiral.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-elphinstone-erskine.jpg" alt="James Elphinstone Erskine" width="305" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:James_Elphinstone_Erskine.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
